{"hash":"6db4fa3613881c09","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":88.433,"said":"This wide court is the Mandir Chowk of the Shri Kashi Vishwanath Dham. For most of the temple’s life there was nothing like it. Pilgrims reached Baba through narrow, crowded lanes, and the temple’s own premises covered only about three thousand square feet. Then, on the thirteenth of December 2021, the Dham was opened: about five lakh square feet of courts, galleries and steps, joining the temple directly to the riverfront at Lalita Ghat. Something remarkable happened while it was being built. Around three hundred old properties were acquired, and as the houses came down, more than forty ancient temples were found hidden inside them, swallowed over the centuries by the growing city. They have been restored, and you can see some of them around the Dham today. This court has become a meeting place too. Since 2022 the Kashi Tamil Sangamam has brought visitors from Tamil Nadu here, to celebrate an old bond between this city and the far south. You will understand that bond better in a few minutes, because it runs from this river to a temple on the southern sea. Look ahead, past the galleries, to where the ground falls away. That is the Ganga Dwar, the river gate. Let us go down.\n\nDid you know? The Dham was planned to let some fifty to seventy-five thousand devotees reach the temple and its courts.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1192},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1208,"end":1313}],"words":[[0.098,0.3,0,4],[0.411,0.288,5,9],[0.711,0.3,10,15],[1.024,0.12,16,18],[1.156,0.108,19,22],[1.276,0.421,23,29],[1.709,0.325,30,35],[2.045,0.108,36,38],[2.165,0.12,39,42],[2.298,0.276,43,47],[2.586,0.445,48,53],[3.043,0.601,54,64],[3.656,0.385,65,69],[4.964,0.156,71,74],[5.132,0.325,75,79],[5.469,0.072,80,82],[5.553,0.108,83,86],[5.673,0.529,87,95],[6.214,0.3,96,100],[6.526,0.144,101,106],[6.683,0.168,107,110],[6.863,0.373,111,118],[7.248,0.24,119,123],[7.5,0.264,124,126],[8.6